Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: You should not take venlafaxine if you are allergic to it or to desvenlafaxine (Pristiq).
Do not use venlafaxine if you have used an MAO inhibitor in the past 14 days. A dangerous drug interaction could occur. MAO inhibitors include isocarboxazid, linezolid, methylene blue injection, phenelzine, and tranylcypromine.
Tell your doctor if you also use stimulant medicine, opioid medicine, herbal products, or medicine for depression, mental illness, Parkinson's disease, migraine headaches, serious infections, or prevention of nausea and vomiting. An interaction with venlafaxine could cause a serious condition called serotonin syndrome.
To make sure venlafaxine is safe for you, tell your doctor if you have ever had:
- bipolar disorder (manic depression);
- heart disease, high blood pressure, high cholesterol or triglycerides, or a stroke;
- diabetes;
- lung disease;
- glaucoma;
- a thyroid disorder;
- a seizure;
- sexual problems;
- bleeding problems;
- low blood levels of sodium; or
- liver or kidney disease.
Triplet: ["venlafaxine", "has interaction warning", "serotonin syndrome"]

The relation 'has interaction warning' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug may cause a specific adverse interaction or condition when used with other substances or in certain situations, as specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'has side effect': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect or symptom specified by the object entity.
B. 'interacts with': The subject drug has a drug interaction with the drug or substance specified by the object entity that may change effects or cause harm.
C. 'has side effect frequency': The subject drug may cause the adverse effect specified by the object entity with the frequency indicated.
D. 'has related drug': The subject drug is related to or associated with another drug specified by the object entity.
E. 'has side effect resolution': The subject drug's side effect may resolve under the condition specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
